      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to convert the base 7 numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base 10, perform the multiplication in base 10, and then convert the result back to base 7. Finally, we will find the sum of the digits of the resulting number in base 7.\n\n1. Convert \\(24_7\\) to base 10:\n\\[24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\\]\n\n2. Convert \\(30_7\\) to base 10:\n\\[30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}\\]\n\n3. Multiply the base 10 numbers:\n\\[18_{10} \\cdot 21_{10} = 378_{10}\\]\n\n4. Convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base 7:\nTo convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base 7, we divide by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\\[378 \\div 7 = 54 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\\]\n\\[54 \\div 7 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 5\\]\n\\[7 \\div 7 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\\]\n\\[1 \\div 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\\]\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(378_{10} = 1050_7\\).\n\n5. Find the sum of the digits of \\(1050_7\\):\n\\[1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6\\]\n\nThus, the base 7 sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
