      "text": "To find the product of the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\), we first need to convert these numbers to base ten.\n\nThe number \\(24_7\\) in base ten is:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18\n\\]\nThe number \\(30_7\\) in base ten is:\n\\[\n3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21\n\\]\nNow, we multiply these two base ten numbers:\n\\[\n18 \\times 21 = 378\n\\]\nNext, we need to convert the product \\(378\\) back to base seven. We do this by finding the largest power of 7 that fits into 378 and then breaking it down step by step.\n\nThe largest power of 7 less than or equal to 378 is \\(7^3 = 343\\). So, we have:\n\\[\n378 = 7^3 + 15\n\\]\nWe need to express 15 in terms of powers of 7. The next largest power of 7 less than 15 is \\(7^2 = 49\\), so:\n\\[\n15 = 7^2 + 8\n\\]\nWe need to express 8 in terms of powers of 7. The next largest power of 7 less than 8 is \\(7^1 = 7\\), so:\n\\[\n8 = 7 + 1\n\\]\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n15 = 7^2 + 7^1 + 7^0\n\\]\nTherefore:\n\\[\n378 = 7^3 + 7^2 + 7^1 + 7^0 = 7^3 + 4 \\cdot 7^2 + 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 1 \\cdot 7^0\n\\]\nConverting this to base seven, we get:\n\\[\n378_{10} = 1224_7\n\\]\nNow, we sum the digits of \\(1224_7\\):\n\\[\n1 + 2 + 2 + 4 = 9\n\\]\nThus, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
